# Singularity Tester Installer

This repository is a Windows-first C#/.NET 8 WPF application that helps non-technical users install test APKs onto Meta Quest headsets and Android phones.

Primary goals:
- Novice-friendly wizard UX.
- Deterministic device detection and install flow.
- Clear recovery actions for common ADB/package failures.
- Strict architecture separation: UI -> Core abstractions -> Infrastructure.
- Small, additive changes only. Do not rewrite unrelated files.

Working rules:
- Read `.cursor/plans/master-implementation-plan.md` before major work.
- Follow project architecture documents in `docs/`.
- Testers download `SingularityApkInstaller-win-x64-setup.exe` from GitHub Releases; keep that stable filename on every release.
- Prefer typed models and services over stringly-typed glue code.
- Keep logic out of XAML code-behind except view wiring.
- Never place raw adb command assembly in ViewModels.
- Before finishing any task, run or document acceptance checks.
- When uncertain, choose the smaller implementation that preserves extensibility.

Output expectations:
- Summarize plan first.
- Then implement.
- End with changed files, verification status, and remaining risks/TODOs.